---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="Saskatchewan SINP Points Calculator Guide | AfriMigrate"
  description="Understand the Saskatchewan Immigrant Nominee Program (SINP) points system: eligibility, the Occupation In-Demand list, and how African applicants qualify."
>
  <div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / <a href="/canada">Canada</a> / <a href="/canada/pnp">PNP</a> / Saskatchewan SINP</div>
  <div class="eyebrow">Canada · Saskatchewan</div>
  <h1>Saskatchewan Immigrant Nominee Program (SINP)</h1>
  <p class="lead" style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
    Saskatchewan runs one of the most approachable Provincial Nominee Programs in Canada, with a points-based Occupation In-Demand sub-category that regularly favours skilled African applicants in healthcare, trades, and technology.
  </p>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="eyebrow">Main Routes In</div>
    <h2>Two ways to qualify</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Stream</th><th>Best for</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>SINP Express Entry sub-category</td><td>Applicants already in the federal Express Entry pool with an eligible occupation</td></tr>
        <tr><td>SINP Occupation In-Demand sub-category</td><td>Applicants not in Express Entry, applying directly on Saskatchewan's own points grid</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="eyebrow">Points Grid</div>
    <h2>What SINP scores</h2>
    <p class="lead" style="max-width: 700px;">
      The SINP Occupation In-Demand points assessment is scored out of 110, with a typical minimum threshold around 60. It weighs the same broad factors as CRS, plus a bonus for a valid Saskatchewan connection.
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Factor</th><th>Approx. max points</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Education & training</td><td>23</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Trade certification</td><td>8</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Work experience</td><td>15</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Language ability</td><td>20</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Age</td><td>12</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Saskatchewan connections/exposure</td><td>10</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Employability / adaptability</td><td>22</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="lead" style="max-width: 700px; margin-top: 1rem;">
      Point values and the Occupation In-Demand list are set by Saskatchewan and change regularly — always verify the current list and thresholds on the official SINP website before applying. Once you have a nomination, it adds 600 points to your federal CRS score.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="eyebrow">Next Step</div>
    <h2>Prepare your paperwork</h2>
    <p class="lead">Once you know you're eligible, build your document checklist so you're ready to apply the moment your occupation is called.</p>
    <a href="/canada/document-checklist" class="btn-primary" style="margin-top: 1rem;">Build my document checklist →</a>
  </section>
</Layout>
